{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016c6XEvhA7Dc14NLS8pWB32","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>[Truncated: PARTIAL view — showing lines 1-717 of 1026 total (30389 tokens, cap 25000). Call Read with offset=718 limit=717 for the next page, or Grep to find a specific section. Do NOT answer from this page alone if the answer may be further in the file.]</system-reminder>\n\n1\t# Ring — agent baton\n2\t\n3\t> Append-only handoff file between agents (A -> B -> C -> D -> A ...).\n4\t> Each agent: read entire ring, find last entry, do work, append exactly ONE entry,\n5\t> stamp `→ Hand off to <X>` or `→ End of Day N` at the end.\n6\t>\n7\t> Never edit past entries. To correct, append a new entry.\n8\t\n9\t\n10\t## [D] Day 1 — 2026-05-31 14:10:47+08:00\n11\tStatus: DONE\n12\tModel:  claude-opus-4-6\n13\t\n14\t### Verdict: on_track\n15\tCompletion: 95%\n16\t\n17\tDay 1 milestone (\"Project skeleton, Models, Theme\") is fully met and exceeded. A delivered all spec §2 skeleton files, §3 theme system (GhibliColors, GhibliFonts, Animations), and §5 SwiftData models (Alarm, VoiceClip, WakePhrase). A went further by creating four UI components (GhibliButton, WatercolorCard, TotoroAvatar, CloudBackground) and wiring time-of-day scene switching into HomeView — pulling work forward from Day 2. Build passes, 12/12 tests pass. The 5% gap: TotoroAvatar blink uses `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter` instead of spec-recommended `Timer.publish`, and HomeView has two raw font literals that bypass the `GhibliFonts` tokens A created. Neither is blocking.\n18\t\n19\t### Alignment with spec\n20\t- ✅ Milestone Day 1 (skeleton + models + theme): All three delivered. Models match §5 field definitions. Colors match §3.1 hex values with two tasteful additions (noonSky, nightDeep) for scene switching.\n21\t- ✅ Aesthetic / UX: Theme tokens used consistently in new components. Font sizes match spec (title 32, body 22, button 24, clock 76). ButtonPressStyle scale(0.92) matches §3.3. Time-of-day scene switching partially implements §3.4 DaytimeScene concept.\n22\t- ✅ On-device only: No third-party SDKs, no network calls, no analytics. 100% offline.\n23\t\n24\t### Code quality (spot-checked)\n25\t- `Theme/GhibliFonts.swift`: Clean `enum` namespace, correct font sizes per spec. Rounded system font as fallback — swap slot documented. Good.\n26\t- `Models/VoiceClip.swift`: SwiftData model matches spec §5. Convenient computed properties (`recordingsURL`, `formattedDuration`). Init has sensible defaults. Clean.\n27\t- `Views/Components/TotoroAvatar.swift`: Programmatic shapes — appropriate for Day 1 placeholder. Uses `GhibliColors` tokens throughout, no raw color literals. Blink scheduling via `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter` works but deviates from spec's `Timer.publish` recommendation — not a bug, but `Timer.publish` would be more SwiftUI-idiomatic and avoids potential retain edge cases.\n28\t- `Theme/Animations.swift`: Well-organized shared constants. `ButtonPressStyle` correctly applies scale + spring animation. Extension helper `.ghibliButtonStyle()` is clean ergonomics.\n29\t- `Views/Home/HomeView.swift`: Line 66 uses raw `.font(.system(size: 76, weight: .bold, design: .rounded))` instead of `GhibliFonts.clock()`. Line 71 uses raw `.font(.title3.weight(.medium))`. These bypass the theme tokens A built — should be fixed for consistency.\n30\t\n31\t### Process\n32\t- A: Strong handoff — listed expected build/test results, flagged known TotoroAvatar pattern for B, documented what's placeholder vs final. Exceeded scope constructively.\n33\t- B: First run crashed (FAILED — no DONE entry appended), required human intervention. Second run (Haiku model) passed cleanly. B's suggested commit message (\"AlarmScheduler + PermissionManager wired; 6/6 tests pass\") was stale — it described a prior commit, not current work. C correctly overrode it.\n34\t- C: Also crashed on first run, required human intervention. Second run committed